# Code owners for the keepcrypt repo. Today only the KeepCrypt-Entropy project (Entropy/) and
# its CI are listed; its owner and security contact is admin@keepcrypt.com (Entropy/SECURITY.md).
# GitHub honours an email owner only if it is a verified email of an account with write access
# to this repo; `gh api repos/bitwilll/keepcrypt/codeowners/errors` lists any problem.
#
# This file says who must review, not how many. GitHub accepts an approval from any one owner
# on a line. The two approvals for Entropy/core/, ffi/ and pi/os/ come from branch protection on
# main (required approving reviews = 2), not from this file.
#
# Syntax, from GitHub's "About code owners" (github/docs commit 0b183d5):
# - patterns follow gitignore rules, except that "!" negation, "[ ]" ranges and "\#" escapes
#   do not work
# - order matters: the last matching pattern wins, so the gate files come last
# - paths are case sensitive; a line with invalid syntax is skipped
# - GitHub reads .github/CODEOWNERS before a root or docs/ copy; /.github/ is owned below

# Security-critical code (docs/build-plan.md, "Security rules enforced in CI": Review).
/Entropy/core/          admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/ffi/           admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/pi/os/         admin@keepcrypt.com
# hal::HwRng (raw /dev/hwrng for the health tests) and the ceremony.
/Entropy/pi/app/        admin@keepcrypt.com
# Rule 9: no INTERNET permission (the Android app arrives in M5).
/Entropy/mobile/**/AndroidManifest.xml  admin@keepcrypt.com

# Known-answer gate: test vectors and the offline verifier that checks them.
/Entropy/vectors/       admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/tools/verify/  admin@keepcrypt.com

# The rules every session follows, the domain constants (CLAUDE.md), the spec and the lessons.
/Entropy/CLAUDE.md          admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/docs/              admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/tasks/lessons.md   admin@keepcrypt.com
# Where vulnerability reports go.
/Entropy/SECURITY.md        admin@keepcrypt.com

# Gate files, so a gate cannot be weakened unseen.
# Toolchain pin and lockfile. rustup prefers a legacy rust-toolchain file over the .toml pin.
/Entropy/rust-toolchain.toml        admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/rust-toolchain             admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/Cargo.lock                 admin@keepcrypt.com
# Manifests: features (test-sources, rule 10), [patch] and [lints] do not show in Cargo.lock.
/Entropy/**/Cargo.toml               admin@keepcrypt.com
# Cargo config can replace crates.io, add rustflags or set CLIPPY_CONF_DIR. Cargo also reads it
# from parent directories, so this matches .cargo/ anywhere in the repo, the root included.
.cargo/                     admin@keepcrypt.com
# cargo-deny reads any of these next to the manifest (Entropy/) or in a parent.
/Entropy/deny.toml                  admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/.deny.toml                 admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/deny.exceptions.toml       admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/.deny.exceptions.toml      admin@keepcrypt.com
# Clippy reads either name from a crate dir or any parent (core/clippy.toml, ffi/clippy.toml).
/Entropy/**/clippy.toml              admin@keepcrypt.com
/Entropy/**/.clippy.toml             admin@keepcrypt.com
# Banned-API gate, canaries and their fixtures.
/Entropy/scripts/                   admin@keepcrypt.com
# cargo vet audits and exemptions.
/Entropy/supply-chain/              admin@keepcrypt.com
# Keeps keys, secrets and ceremony backups out of git (rule 12).
/Entropy/.gitignore                 admin@keepcrypt.com
# CI workflows and this file (the Entropy workflow is .github/workflows/entropy-ci.yml).
/.github/                   admin@keepcrypt.com
